 ;; ── ROUND 4: invoke-equivalence gate (the REAL quality gate) ──────────────
 ;;   build-pass != runtime-correct. Deploy agent.wasm to live :8077, invoke with the
 ;;   same input as the original cell's solve(), compare output state dicts.
 ;;   harness: invoke_equiv.py · raw: results/invoke-equiv.json
 :round4-invoke-equiv
 {:status :done
  :scope "2 no-relative-import cells (service-request, final-sign-off) x claude + gemini"
  :contract "POST :8077/mcp kotoba_wasm_run {wasm_b64, agent_did, program_cid, ctx_cbor_b64};
             ctx CBOR {graph, session_cid, args:{input, thread_id}}; out at result.content[0].text
             (JSON str) -> output_cbor_b64 -> CBOR {ok: json_str}. Auth = JWT, exp-only (no sig)."
  :results {:service-request {:claude :EQUIV :gemini :EQUIV}     ; both runtime-correct
            :final-sign-off  {:claude :MISMATCH :gemini :MISMATCH}}
  :the-find "final-sign-off: BOTH models' ports are runtime-WRONG in one subtle way that build-pass,
             structural-check AND the LLM-judge ALL MISSED — the WASM output carries an EXTRA top-level
             `projectId` key. Cause: the port declares StateGraph(SignOffStateDict) with projectId as a
             typed channel, so the input field persists into the output state; the ORIGINAL uses
             StateGraph(dict) which drops it. This is exactly why invoke-equivalence is the real gate."
  :systematic "Same defect in BOTH claude and gemini → NOT a model differentiator; it's an artifact of the
               migration CONTRACT. Actionable prompt fix: instruct ports to mirror the original's state
               schema (don't promote input keys into the typed TypedDict output) OR accept benign
               passthrough via a normalized comparison."
  :infra-bug-found "The running :8077 binary caches the compiled program by AGENT_DID, not program_cid —
                    the ADR-2605310200 fix is in SOURCE but NOT in the deployed binary. Symptom: every
                    invoke with the same DID returned the FIRST wasm's output. Worked around in invoke_equiv.py
                    with a unique agent_did per wasm; the deployed kotoba binary should be rebuilt."}

 ;; ── ROUND 5: hardening items 1-4 (post-gemini-selection) ──────────────────
 :round5-hardening
 {:item1-prompt-fix
  {:status :done-with-deeper-find
   :did "added a StateGraph(dict) rule to the migration prompt; re-migrated final-sign-off (gemini)
         — source now uses StateGraph(dict) not a TypedDict."
   :real-root-cause "The projectId leak is NOT a prompt/port issue. kotoba_langgraph/graph.py:175
                     `_apply_update(state, input_state, schema)` merges the FULL input dict into state
                     and never drops unwritten channels — unlike real langgraph (which keeps only
                     declared/written channels). So the WASM retains projectId even with StateGraph(dict)."
   :resolution "invoke_equiv.py now reports TWO verdicts: strict (byte-exact) and
                equivalence-modulo-input-passthrough (all gold keys match AND extra keys ⊆ input keys).
                Result: 2/4 strict, 4/4 modulo-input. The only divergence is the documented substrate
                quirk, not a model defect."
   :substrate-fix-LANDED
   {:where "40-engine/kotoba/py/kotoba_langgraph/graph.py (kotoba submodule)"
    :what "added _declared_channels() + _prune_dynamic_channels(); invoke()/stream() now track
           node-written keys and, for dynamic StateGraph(dict) graphs, DROP input-only keys that no
           node writes — matching real langgraph. Typed-schema graphs keep declared channels (parity)."
    :tests "py/tests/test_dynamic_channels.py (4 new, green); full suite 100 passed (1 pre-existing
            asyncio-plugin failure, unrelated)."
    :result "after the substrate fix + #1 prompt fix + rebuild, ALL functional-cell ports are now
             STRICT-equivalent to their originals: invoke-equiv = 4/4 STRICT (service-request +
             final-sign-off, x claude + gemini). The projectId divergence is fully resolved."
    :followup "commit the kotoba submodule change + bump the parent submodule pointer."}}

